meta {
  name: Register All With Exchange
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/siteadmin/tenants/register-exchange
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{siteAdminToken}}
}

docs {
  Register every tenant that has an `exchangeTenantId` but is not yet registered
  as a client on the external Exchange server (the `POST /clients` step). This is
  the prerequisite that lets the Exchange attribute per-tenant message counts.
  SiteAdmin only — requires `system:config` (super_owner). No request body.

  Idempotent: already-registered tenants (those with `exchangeRegisteredAt` set)
  are skipped by the query. Sequential; a per-tenant failure is logged + counted
  and does not abort the batch. Reuses each tenant's `exchangeTenantId` as
  `peer_tenant_id` — never creates a new/conflicting id.

  Run `sync-exchange-ids` first so every tenant has an `exchangeTenantId`.

  Returns in `data`:
  - `registered` — count freshly registered this run.
  - `failed` — count that errored.
  - `failures` — array of `{ tenantId, error }` for the failures.
}
